/* Frappe's own core print_format.css (shared by every print format, not
   specific to this one) floats the page as a narrower white block
   centered on a grey backdrop while VIEWING it on screen - that's where
   the side margins in an on-screen preview come from, separately from
   this format's own @page margins above (which control the actual
   printed/PDF output and are already 0). Overridden here so the on-
   screen preview also fills the available width instead of leaving that
   same empty space visible before anything is even printed. Scoped to
   @media screen only, so it has zero effect on the actual PDF. */
@media screen {
  body {
    max-width: 100% !important;
    min-width: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    box-shadow: none !important;
  }
}

