     table) regardless of the widths set here. */
  table-layout: fixed;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  margin-bottom: 18px;
  font-size: 10.5px;
}

.bsi-table th,
.bsi-table td {
  /* No row is allowed to wrap onto a second line, no matter how long the
     Keterangan text is - overflow gets truncated with an ellipsis instead
     (title="" on the cell repeats the full text so it's not lost, just
     not fully visible on paper). */
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

/* No/Tanggal/Deposit/Withdrawal/Balance get fixed px widths, sized to
   comfortably fit their actual longest content ("2026-05-15", "9,999,999.99")
   regardless of how wide the table itself ends up being - percentages
   were the original bug here: at 4%/9% of the table's width, the padding
   below (8-10px each side) alone ate nearly the whole column, leaving no
   room for even "No"/"Tanggal" to render past 2-3 characters before the
   ellipsis kicked in. Keterangan is left with no explicit width on
   purpose - table-layout: fixed hands 100% of whatever's left over to the
   one column that doesn't have a set width, which is exactly the "let
   the long free-text column absorb the remaining space" behavior wanted
   here. */
.bsi-table th:nth-child(1),
.bsi-table td:nth-child(1) { width: 42px; }
.bsi-table th:nth-child(2),
.bsi-table td:nth-child(2) { width: 78px; }
.bsi-table th:nth-child(4),
.bsi-table td:nth-child(4) { width: 88px; }
.bsi-table th:nth-child(5),
.bsi-table td:nth-child(5) { width: 88px; }
.bsi-table th:nth-child(6),
.bsi-table td:nth-child(6) { width: 98px; }

.bsi-table thead th {
