/* calc() combined with table-layout:fixed on the SAME <table> is what's
   unreliable in wkhtmltopdf - not calc() alone (.pop-items-table's own
   width below uses calc() fine, but it's auto-layout, not fixed) and not
   table-layout:fixed alone (plain % column widths work) - only the two
   together, confirmed by an actual wkhtmltopdf render where this exact
   combination silently produced a too-narrow table. The margin/calc
   width now lives on a plain wrapping <div> instead (no layout mode to
   conflict with), and the inner table is a plain width:100% fixed-layout
   table with nothing to resolve but its own columns. */
